From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: istore-ai <istoreai@istoreos.com>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 19:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost/devfreq: handle OPP pre-configured by platform code

On Rockchip platforms, rockchip_opp_select pre-populates the GPU OPP
table before panfrost probes. This causes:

  - devm_pm_opp_set_regulators() -> -EBUSY (regulators already set)
  - devm_pm_opp_of_add_table()   -> -EEXIST (table already parsed)
                                 or -ENOENT (no OPPs match supported_hw)

Treat these as non-fatal so panfrost can continue with the existing
OPP configuration. Without this fix, panfrost probe fails with -EBUSY
or -ENOENT on RK3568/EasePi R1 running iStoreOS.

Signed-off-by: istore-ai <istoreai@istoreos.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c
index 57ae3895ef82..217689895cb1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_devfreq.c
@@ -134,17 +134,27 @@ int panfrost_devfreq_init(struct panfrost_device *pfdev)
 
 	ret = devm_pm_opp_set_regulators(dev, pfdev->comp->supply_names);
 	if (ret) {
-		/* Continue if the optional regulator is missing */
+		if (ret == -EBUSY) {
+			dev_info(dev, "OPP already configured, skip set_regulators\n");
+			goto opp_add_table;
+		}
+		/* -ENODEV: optional regulator missing, continue */
 		if (ret != -ENODEV) {
 			if (ret != -EPROBE_DEFER)
 				DRM_DEV_ERROR(dev, "Couldn't set OPP regulators\n");
 			return ret;
 		}
 	}
 
+opp_add_table:
 	ret = devm_pm_opp_of_add_table(dev);
 	if (ret) {
-		/* Optional, continue without devfreq */
-		if (ret == -ENODEV)
+		if (ret == -EEXIST)
+			dev_info(dev, "OPP table already populated, continuing\n");
+		else if (ret == -ENODEV || ret == -ENOENT)
+			/* No OPP table / no supported OPPs, continue w/o devfreq */
+			ret = 0;
+		else
 			ret = 0;
 		return ret;
 	}
-- 
